WEBVTT

01:31.216 --> 01:34.052
Do you remember
the last thing that you said to me?

01:38.640 --> 01:40.100
"She's alive."

01:42.227 --> 01:44.313
Have you finished Cold Harbor?

01:48.567 --> 01:50.110
What is this place?

01:50.611 --> 01:52.571
It's a cabin for giving birth.

01:55.282 --> 01:57.700
Why am I here? Why are you here?

01:57.701 --> 01:59.244
Cold Harbor.

01:59.745 --> 02:01.538
Have you finished it?

02:05.876 --> 02:06.919
No.

02:09.128 --> 02:11.548
Then she's still alive.

02:13.133 --> 02:15.093
We can save her.

02:16.720 --> 02:17.596
Who?

02:19.223 --> 02:20.641
Ms. Casey.

02:21.683 --> 02:22.684
Gemma.

02:25.229 --> 02:29.399
There's a hallway down there.
It's different than the others.

02:30.067 --> 02:32.319
It's long and black and hidden.

02:34.571 --> 02:36.198
From Irving's drawings.

02:37.699 --> 02:38.784
What?

02:40.911 --> 02:43.038
With an elevator going down.

02:46.458 --> 02:47.835
We know where it is.

02:55.467 --> 02:58.470
What a funny speech you gave at the party.

03:06.270 --> 03:08.772
I was cross with you after.

03:12.860 --> 03:15.153
I threw a tin of candies.

03:19.366 --> 03:21.577
God, you're fucking weird.

03:47.060 --> 03:49.563
I do not love my daughter.

03:54.443 --> 03:57.154
I used to see Kier in her,

03:58.739 --> 04:00.991
but he left her as she grew.

04:04.161 --> 04:05.871
You sound like a great dad.

04:07.748 --> 04:10.209
I sired others in the shadows.

04:12.294 --> 04:14.379
But he wasn't in them either.

04:19.760 --> 04:21.887
Until I saw him again.

04:25.265 --> 04:26.391
In you.

04:29.186 --> 04:31.897
You and your family created hell,
and you're going to burn in it.

04:41.323 --> 04:42.824
There he is.

04:45.702 --> 04:48.080
Tomorrow is a special day.

04:51.834 --> 04:52.835
Hey!

04:55.128 --> 04:56.839
Why did you come here?

04:57.840 --> 04:59.508
What do you want from me?

05:03.428 --> 05:06.347
So, wait, when I finish Cold Harbor,

05:06.348 --> 05:10.768
they do a test, and then they kill her?

05:10.769 --> 05:16.357
Once that file is done, you'll need
to quickly get to the black hallway,

05:16.358 --> 05:18.317
then down to the testing floor.

05:18.318 --> 05:22.322
They'll not let you leave MDR
till that file is complete.

05:23.073 --> 05:25.533
Okay, but how do I find her
once I'm down there?

05:25.534 --> 05:26.701
No, you won't.

05:26.702 --> 05:28.119
- I won't?
- No.

05:28.120 --> 05:31.707
Your chip is only attuned to your floor.

05:32.207 --> 05:35.252
Once you get down to testing,
you'll be your outie again.

05:36.670 --> 05:39.505
And then he'll find Gemma
and take her up to the severed floor.

05:39.506 --> 05:43.468
Where you will guide her
to the exit stairwell.

05:46.054 --> 05:47.097
Right. Okay.

05:50.100 --> 05:51.185
Mark...

05:53.061 --> 05:55.606
I know this is a fucking lot, man.

05:57.733 --> 05:59.942
But if we can prove that she is alive,

05:59.943 --> 06:02.696
if we can prove
that they fucking kidnapped her,

06:03.947 --> 06:05.449
it will end them.

06:14.374 --> 06:17.044
Well, what happens to us?

06:18.712 --> 06:19.796
What do you mean?

06:22.966 --> 06:28.388
Well, if Lumon ends, then what happens
to every innie on the severed floor?

06:33.352 --> 06:34.269
Yeah.

06:46.490 --> 06:48.866
- You want me to give my life?
- No.

06:48.867 --> 06:50.660
The lives of everyone down there?

06:50.661 --> 06:52.454
No, it's not that simple.

06:54.623 --> 06:57.668
Just to save one person
you happen to care about?

06:58.794 --> 07:01.505
It doesn't have to end your life.

07:04.842 --> 07:05.884
Really?

07:07.344 --> 07:08.345
Right.

07:10.097 --> 07:13.058
There's somebody else
who wants to talk to you, actually.

07:25.612 --> 07:29.700
Okay, just hit the play.

07:43.755 --> 07:44.923
Watch it.

07:46.091 --> 07:50.971
Record your response, then step outside.

07:53.932 --> 07:55.516
We'll just be downstairs, okay?

07:55.517 --> 07:56.602
Okay.

08:19.708 --> 08:22.169
Hey, I'm...

08:22.836 --> 08:24.546
Well, I guess you know who I am.

08:25.881 --> 08:28.424
I think you've spoken
with Devon and Mrs. Sel...

08:28.425 --> 08:29.927
Ms. Cobel.

08:32.221 --> 08:33.347
So y...

08:33.931 --> 08:36.725
you know what it is that we're asking.

08:38.644 --> 08:40.729
But the first thing I need to say to you

08:41.230 --> 08:45.526
is that I am so sorry.

08:46.693 --> 08:52.199
You know, I created you
as a prisoner and as an escape.

08:53.450 --> 08:57.245
Lumon told me you'd be happy,
that innies are content,

08:57.246 --> 08:59.330
and because I took their word for it,

08:59.331 --> 09:01.708
you've been living a nightmare
for two years.

09:04.294 --> 09:06.338
It's horrific what they've done to you.

09:06.964 --> 09:12.636
And part of the reason I'm here
is to make it right.

09:14.388 --> 09:18.516
And I hope now with all we have in common,

09:18.517 --> 09:22.104
that you'll give me that chance.

10:47.272 --> 10:48.315
Hi.

10:50.817 --> 10:53.611
Wow, this is...
I never expected to actually speak to you.

10:53.612 --> 10:55.030
Holy shit.

10:55.656 --> 10:58.742
Let alone get an apology, so...

11:01.828 --> 11:02.829
Thank you.

11:05.582 --> 11:09.253
You know, "nightmare"
is the wrong word, actually.

11:11.213 --> 11:14.591
'Cause we find ways to make it work, to...

11:15.884 --> 11:17.469
to feel whole,

11:19.137 --> 11:21.682
which is why what you're asking scares me.

11:22.808 --> 11:26.603
You know, because whatever this life is...

11:28.021 --> 11:29.857
it's all we have,

11:30.440 --> 11:33.402
and we don't want it to end.

11:34.069 --> 11:35.529
Can you understand that?

12:06.351 --> 12:07.686
Of course I can.

12:08.187 --> 12:09.730
It's such a good point.

12:10.606 --> 12:14.985
I'd say the same thing
in your position, however,

12:16.904 --> 12:20.991
Lumon doesn't have to be your whole life.

12:22.576 --> 12:25.828
Now, you may have been
seeing flashes lately.

12:25.829 --> 12:28.039
Images from my world out here.

12:28.040 --> 12:29.958
I've been seeing yours too.

12:30.834 --> 12:34.754
It's a process called "reintegration."

12:34.755 --> 12:39.092
It's a way to recouple memories
so we can be one person.

12:40.385 --> 12:44.138
I started this because I see now
how unfair this all is to you,

12:44.139 --> 12:48.852
and once my wife is free,
I swear I will finish the process.

12:50.521 --> 12:52.314
'Cause this life, our life...

12:54.149 --> 12:55.901
belongs to both of us.

12:57.569 --> 12:59.905
And I wanna share it with you.

13:11.291 --> 13:14.168
Okay. But what would that mean exactly?

13:14.169 --> 13:18.465
That you get the right side,
and I get the left? Or...

13:19.424 --> 13:20.842
Is it like a top-bottom situation? I'm--

13:20.843 --> 13:22.510
- No.
- I'm honestly trying to understand.

13:22.511 --> 13:25.596
No, it wouldn't be like
a top-bottom situation.

13:25.597 --> 13:29.475
It's, like, both of us.
Like, one person combined.

13:29.476 --> 13:34.480
Like, my memories and yours,
and my trauma and yours,

13:34.481 --> 13:36.650
but, like, you know, the good stuff too.

13:40.821 --> 13:42.030
Okay, but...

13:42.781 --> 13:47.159
I mean, you've been alive for, what,
20 times longer,

13:47.160 --> 13:51.455
so whoever this new hybrid person is,

13:51.456 --> 13:55.002
it seems like
he'd be way more you than me.

13:59.214 --> 14:01.008
I just don't think that's how it works.

14:03.093 --> 14:05.012
Okay. How does it work?

14:28.243 --> 14:29.244
Look...

14:33.332 --> 14:37.252
I mourned Gemma for two years.

14:43.050 --> 14:46.345
I lost my job, my teaching job...

14:48.931 --> 14:53.435
because I fucking started
showing up drunk.

15:00.150 --> 15:03.153
You know, I hid all of her stuff
in my basement...

15:05.364 --> 15:08.158
'cause it was easier pretending
that she never existed.

15:14.081 --> 15:16.583
And I thought I was protecting you
from that pain.

15:25.926 --> 15:30.764
Hey, Ms. Cobel told me
you like someone down there?

15:32.975 --> 15:35.059
Helena Eagan, right?

15:35.060 --> 15:37.312
I think her innie name's "Heleny"?

15:39.314 --> 15:42.401
Honestly,
I love that you had that experience.

15:44.069 --> 15:47.113
So, now you could imagine,

15:47.114 --> 15:49.116
like, what you and Heleny have

15:49.825 --> 15:53.411
but multiply, like, thousands of days

15:53.412 --> 15:57.832
of, like, joy, and arguments, and passion,

15:57.833 --> 16:01.502
then you can see why
I have to get my wife back.

16:01.503 --> 16:03.255
I have to have her back.

16:25.485 --> 16:27.738
It's Helly, actually. Helly.

16:31.116 --> 16:32.910
It's the person I'm in love with,

16:33.744 --> 16:36.954
which you'd know if you'd ever
taken an interest in my life.

16:36.955 --> 16:39.333
Before tonight, when you need something.

16:41.335 --> 16:45.338
She's the person I'll lose
if I do what you say

16:45.339 --> 16:50.761
'cause you know as well as I do
that her outie won't, like, reintegrate,

16:52.721 --> 16:54.473
assuming that's even real.

16:55.182 --> 16:57.893
Assuming every word
outta your mouth isn't a lie.

16:58.393 --> 16:59.603
Wha...

17:03.398 --> 17:05.400
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to...

17:06.652 --> 17:09.819
Dude, I'm just trying
to save my wife, okay?

17:09.820 --> 17:13.574
I mean, I can't abandon her,
and if you help me,

17:13.575 --> 17:16.369
I won't abandon you. I promise.

17:17.663 --> 17:20.539
You know what I think? I think
the second you get your wife back,

17:20.540 --> 17:22.416
you forget I ever existed.

17:23.001 --> 17:27.005
I think that I disappear
along with every innie down there.

17:28.423 --> 17:29.674
What do you want from me?

17:29.675 --> 17:31.634
We are in this together.

17:31.635 --> 17:34.096
Can't you just trust me?

17:38.350 --> 17:39.351
No.

17:41.937 --> 17:43.313
Devon!

17:43.814 --> 17:46.566
He's a fucking child. He won't listen.

17:46.567 --> 17:47.733
Let me speak to him.

17:47.734 --> 17:50.279
I mentioned reintegration,
he basically called bullshit.

17:50.863 --> 17:52.738
Well, he's not wrong, right?

17:52.739 --> 17:54.491
Let me speak to him.

17:56.243 --> 17:57.244
Alone.

17:58.912 --> 18:00.330
Okay. Yeah.

18:08.172 --> 18:09.173
Okay.

18:23.228 --> 18:25.022
The numbers are your wife.

18:32.070 --> 18:34.031
The MDR numbers.

18:34.698 --> 18:35.866
From your console.

18:46.168 --> 18:50.422
They're a doorway into the mind
of your outie's wife, Gemma Scout.

18:56.178 --> 18:57.638
I don't understand.

19:02.392 --> 19:04.603
What do you see every day
when you look at them?

19:13.445 --> 19:17.741
What... we feel things.

19:21.703 --> 19:22.913
What do you feel?

19:25.874 --> 19:29.669
Different things. Sometimes sadness...

19:29.670 --> 19:30.587
Woe.

19:32.756 --> 19:33.590
Frolic.

19:36.051 --> 19:37.594
Malice.

19:39.471 --> 19:40.722
Dread.

19:44.726 --> 19:46.603
So you're saying the...

19:47.604 --> 19:49.272
the clusters are...

19:49.273 --> 19:51.149
Her tempers.

19:53.694 --> 19:56.864
The building blocks of her mind.

19:59.324 --> 20:00.826
What am I building?

20:05.038 --> 20:08.000
Every file you've completed...

20:10.419 --> 20:12.504
is a new consciousness for her.

20:19.094 --> 20:20.762
A new innie.

20:27.519 --> 20:30.063
I've completed 24 files.

20:31.690 --> 20:34.318
Cold Harbor is the last.

20:37.154 --> 20:40.991
Tomorrow will be your final day at Lumon.

20:41.825 --> 20:46.580
You will have served your purpose,
and so will she.

20:58.425 --> 21:00.385
Wait, why are you telling me this?

21:06.225 --> 21:08.435
What are you doing here, really?

21:10.854 --> 21:15.025
Mark. Mark.

21:18.946 --> 21:23.242
There'll be no honeymoon ending
for you and Helly R.

21:26.161 --> 21:28.080
She's an Eagan.

21:30.040 --> 21:32.000
You're nothing to them.

21:32.876 --> 21:34.627
- No.
- Nothing to her.

21:34.628 --> 21:36.128
No, I don't believe you.

21:36.129 --> 21:37.505
They're using you.

21:37.506 --> 21:39.215
No! I don't believe you!

21:39.216 --> 21:41.592
Then they'll discard you like a skin husk.

21:41.593 --> 21:44.345
- I think you're using me!
- Mark!

21:44.346 --> 21:46.848
- Reintegration is your only chance!
- Wait.

21:46.849 --> 21:48.767
- Do you love your brother?
- Mark!

21:49.476 --> 21:50.351
Yes.

21:50.352 --> 21:52.854
Well, then you tell him
that the next thing I see

21:52.855 --> 21:54.480
had better be the severed floor,

21:54.481 --> 21:57.441
or I swear he will never
see his wife again.

21:57.442 --> 21:59.110
I care for you.

21:59.111 --> 22:00.194
Stop!

22:00.195 --> 22:01.321
Mark.

23:11.475 --> 23:12.935
I have to tell you something.

23:13.435 --> 23:14.645
Me too.

24:08.866 --> 24:10.701
Fuck me.

24:59.166 --> 25:04.713
"Mark, The Founder wished to witness
the historic completion of your 25th file.

25:06.173 --> 25:11.136
Helly R. shall also bear witness
from her chair.

25:12.679 --> 25:18.185
Goodly splendors await upon your victory.
Love, Mr. Milchick."

25:59.768 --> 26:01.436
Jame Eagan was here.

26:03.146 --> 26:04.773
He came to see me.

26:06.358 --> 26:10.403
He said some cryptic shit
about the fire of Kier being in me,

26:10.404 --> 26:14.116
and that today is a special day.

26:19.955 --> 26:21.373
I know why.

26:26.420 --> 26:27.963
I know why they're doing this.

26:43.896 --> 26:45.022
Hello, Dylan.

26:47.065 --> 26:48.317
He said no?

26:51.987 --> 26:53.155
Follow me.

27:31.151 --> 27:34.363
So, what happens
when they extract the chip?

27:41.161 --> 27:43.539
But how can we trust anything Cobel says?

27:44.331 --> 27:46.166
All she's ever done is lie.

27:46.667 --> 27:50.128
I know, but she seemed different.

27:50.963 --> 27:56.008
I mean, she's the same, but,
like, different same.

27:56.009 --> 27:57.511
I don't know.

28:03.517 --> 28:05.185
I mean, I could just not do it.

28:06.812 --> 28:09.898
I could just not finish the file,
not get her out.

28:11.191 --> 28:14.027
But if she's telling the truth,
we're screwed either way.

28:21.326 --> 28:22.703
What's happening?

28:23.203 --> 28:24.538
Just get dressed.

28:25.956 --> 28:27.624
Everything is gonna be fine.

28:33.255 --> 28:39.344
But if you get her out, maybe that will
take down Lumon, like his sister said.

28:42.556 --> 28:45.142
And maybe you can do this combining thing.

28:47.019 --> 28:50.147
Well, yeah, but he could be a total liar.

28:51.231 --> 28:52.900
What if he's not?

28:58.447 --> 29:00.324
At least you'll have a chance at living.

29:06.997 --> 29:08.999
Yeah, but I wanna live with you.

29:20.344 --> 29:22.262
But I'm her, Mark.

29:28.977 --> 29:30.354
I'm her.

29:49.915 --> 29:50.916
Okay.

30:37.671 --> 30:40.799
Your outie has responded
to your resignation request.

30:43.719 --> 30:47.139
As it may yield an embarrassing
emotional response in you,

30:47.806 --> 30:49.432
and as I'm duly swamped,

30:49.433 --> 30:52.102
I shall leave you to read it in solitude.

31:18.921 --> 31:20.172
"Dear innie,

31:21.924 --> 31:26.053
I've read your request and organized
my response into three points.

31:26.553 --> 31:29.056
Point one: fuck you."

31:33.185 --> 31:35.812
Gretchen is my wife and my beloved,

31:36.980 --> 31:40.442
and your actions with her
were deeply fucking indecorous.

31:43.278 --> 31:45.030
Point two:

31:47.449 --> 31:48.534
I get it.

31:50.869 --> 31:56.667
She's perfect, and given our shared
physiology, it tracks that you'd agree.

31:58.502 --> 32:00.087
Here's the thing.

32:01.547 --> 32:05.425
I've never been an impressive person,

32:06.802 --> 32:12.724
so when Gretch told me that
you're, like, this self-assured badass,

32:14.101 --> 32:15.185
I don't know.

32:16.645 --> 32:17.729
It stung.

32:20.148 --> 32:22.150
So I guess, point three is:

32:23.902 --> 32:29.157
I hope someday she sees in me
what she sees in you.

32:31.743 --> 32:36.248
In the meantime,
if I'm being really honest,

32:38.333 --> 32:40.043
I guess I like knowing you're there.

32:45.507 --> 32:49.011
So if you wanna leave, you can.

32:50.762 --> 32:53.348
But I think you should stay.

33:00.647 --> 33:03.692
Sincerest regards, Your outie.

33:53.492 --> 33:56.995
Been trying to think
of other place names besides Delaware.

34:01.708 --> 34:07.297
I've got Europe, Zimbabwe...

34:13.387 --> 34:14.888
and the Equator.

34:16.931 --> 34:18.391
The Equator?

34:21.603 --> 34:23.021
Is that a building?

34:24.438 --> 34:26.065
Or a continent.

34:27.900 --> 34:32.238
Maybe it's just a building
that's, like, so big...

34:32.239 --> 34:34.407
That it became a continent.

34:34.408 --> 34:35.742
Yeah.

34:39.246 --> 34:40.664
Yeah.

34:55.971 --> 34:57.931
I just wish we had more time.

35:59.201 --> 36:00.786
Least it's a happy one.

36:41.326 --> 36:42.786
Call Mr. Eagan.

37:27.372 --> 37:29.166
Mark S.,

37:30.959 --> 37:35.839
in completing your 25th Macrodata file,

37:36.965 --> 37:42.846
you have drawn my grand agendum
nearer to fulfillment,

37:43.388 --> 37:46.057
thus making you

37:46.058 --> 37:50.562
one of the most
important people in history.

37:52.481 --> 37:56.485
Revel now in the fruit of your labors,

37:57.110 --> 38:01.364
and hail your earthbound steward,

38:01.365 --> 38:03.575
your very own...

38:04.743 --> 38:09.748
floor manager!

38:19.341 --> 38:21.385
Thank you, Kier.

38:22.469 --> 38:27.682
And may I say,
you're looking very handsome, sir.

38:27.683 --> 38:28.766
Thank you.

38:28.767 --> 38:31.644
I'd say the same of you,

38:31.645 --> 38:34.982
if not for my favorite core principle.

38:36.525 --> 38:37.734
Probity?

38:38.235 --> 38:39.403
No.

38:40.654 --> 38:41.864
Vision.

38:44.658 --> 38:50.163
Well, it's truly special
to host a man so illustrious,

38:50.664 --> 38:54.000
so sapient, so magnanimous--

38:54.001 --> 38:56.461
My, you're verbose.

38:57.296 --> 39:00.716
Good thing you didn't write
the first appendix.

39:01.300 --> 39:02.968
It would've burst.

39:13.937 --> 39:17.858
It's an honor to receive your barbs,
Mr. Eagan.

39:18.483 --> 39:23.946
The legacy you've left behind
is truly and irrefutably larger than life.

39:23.947 --> 39:25.949
You mean my company?

39:28.118 --> 39:29.119
No.

39:31.079 --> 39:35.667
I mean this wax statue that's five inches
taller than you actually were.

39:50.182 --> 39:52.351
Thank you for that feedback...

39:55.354 --> 39:56.688
Seth.

40:00.359 --> 40:01.777
Thank you, Kier.

40:03.529 --> 40:07.698
And now, lady and gentleman of MDR,

40:07.699 --> 40:13.705
may I introduce
Choreography and Merriment!

40:33.725 --> 40:34.852
Let's go.

40:50.701 --> 40:51.785
Mark!

41:26.570 --> 41:28.071
Mark!

41:50.552 --> 41:52.471
Welcome, Mr. Eagan.

41:53.055 --> 41:56.016
The efficacy test will begin shortly.

42:03.148 --> 42:05.692
Thank you, C&M.

42:06.443 --> 42:09.612
Let's keep the Mark S. love going...

42:09.613 --> 42:10.988
I have to leave.

42:10.989 --> 42:13.075
...with the Ballad of Ambrose

42:14.618 --> 42:15.619
and Gunnel.

43:03.876 --> 43:04.877
You ready?

43:07.588 --> 43:08.589
Yeah.

43:10.632 --> 43:12.176
See you at the Equator.

43:14.553 --> 43:16.013
See you at the Equator.

44:14.321 --> 44:17.658
Hey. Can I get a little help?

46:27.287 --> 46:28.288
Hey!

